@chapter 27 | World Population and Urbanization

@intro
The last chapter looks beyond India: **urban sociology** (folk-urban continuum, megalopolis), **world population** (size, distribution, growth, the most populous countries), **density, sex ratio and religion** worldwide, **world urbanization**, **international migration**, and world **fertility and mortality**. Many keys depend on the year asked; the notes give current UN figures. It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 27.1 | Urban Sociology

@q 18:1-3

**Robert Redfield** built the **folk-urban continuum** from studies in **Mexico** (Yucatán); with **Milton Singer** he described **primary urbanization** (growth of a **great tradition**, orthogenetic cities) and secondary urbanization (heterogenetic cities). **Jean Gottmann** coined **megalopolis** (1961) for the Boston-Washington city chain.

