@q 18:62-65

@src1 18:1
@one U.P.P.C.S. (Mains) 2011
In which year was Family Planning Programme started in India?
@ans 1952
@end

**India (1952)** was the first country to adopt an official **national family planning programme**. **Sri Lanka** has South Asia's oldest population. About **80%** of the world's people lack adequate **social security** (ILO). The WDR 2006 ranked **Bangladesh** the poorest of the listed South Asian countries.

@up UP link: The symbolic seven-billionth baby **Nargis** was born at **Mall village, near Lucknow** (31 October 2011). With about 23-24 crore people, UP would rank about **sixth** among the world's countries, just behind Pakistan.

